<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Highest/Lowest Australian P-E Ratios-March 11.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Highest/Lowest Australian P-E Ratios-March 11.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Highest and lowest price earnings ratios for Australian companies included in the 320-company All Ordinaries Index based on closing prices on Monday. P/E based on rolling 12 months earnings.</p>
<p>Highest 10</p>
<p>Rank Name		     P/E    Close</p>
<p> 1   Mayne Nickless	347.93   7.55</p>
<p> 2   Kidston Gold	  293.75   1.41</p>
<p> 3   Mt Edon Gold	  241.76   2.20</p>
<p> 4   St.Barbara Mine     115.49   0.82</p>
<p> 5   Westpac Prop Tr     111.25   1.78</p>
<p> 6   Herald Rsc	     97.35   1.10</p>
<p> 7   Consol Paper	   85.88   2.92</p>
<p> 8   Devex		    83.33   0.38</p>
<p> 9   Tap Oil		  69.89   1.23</p>
<p>10   Goodman Fielder	68.70   1.69</p>
<p>Lowest 10</p>
<p> 1   Dominion Min	    1.95   0.85</p>
<p> 2   Climax Mining	   2.12   1.05</p>
<p> 3   Consol Rutile	   4.64   1.04</p>
<p> 4   BTR Plc		   5.91   5.50</p>
<p> 5   OLS Asia Hldgs	  6.97   0.83</p>
<p> 6   Premier Inv	     7.05   1.25</p>
<p> 7   BT Aust Eq Mgmt	 7.52   0.76</p>
<p> 8   Templeton Global	7.66   1.41</p>
<p> 9   Renison Goldflds	7.82   5.33</p>
<p>10   Aust Gold Rsc	   7.84   1.43</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 373-1800</p>
</text>
